package cosmonic-labs:illustrator-bridge;

/// Host imports this component needs *in addition* to the `wasi:http@0.3.0`
/// service world that the `wasip3` crate generates for us.
///
/// The bridge is a rendezvous between two callers that never meet: an MCP
/// tool call queues a command, and the Illustrator bridge picks it up on its
/// next poll. Those two HTTP requests may land on different component
/// instances, so the queue cannot live in the component's linear memory — it
/// goes in a host keyvalue bucket, which is also what lets the workload run
/// more than one instance (see `poolSize` in workload.yaml).
///
/// Clocks come from `wasi:clocks@0.3.0` via the `wasip3` crate, so they are
/// not repeated here.
world bridge-state {
  import wasi:keyvalue/store@0.2.0-draft;
}
